description:
Project: video-agent, an open-source Netlify template that turns a prompt into a published MP4 via Netlify Agent Runner runs writing HyperFrames compositions; Hono+OpenAPI API, Netlify Database (Drizzle), Blobs, Identity, React+Mantine UI, MCP. Feature: redo a scene (a scoped revision: pick one or more scenes (beats) of a finished version, say what should change, and get a new version where only those scenes changed; everything else is frozen, spliced back deterministically and checked twice, in the run and in finalize). Spec: docs/plans/2026-11-04-regenerate-beat.md (draft 3, commit e477294; review logs at its end, §13). Line refs are as of e477294; main keeps moving (videos.ts, app.ts, schemas.ts, mcp.ts and the UI pages drifted by 4c573aa), so search by the named symbol when a line is off.
Spec key: 2.5
Spec section(s): §4.2 'Older versions', §4.1 'No archive I/O in the transaction', reviews R3, R8, A6

## Background
No read route returns a version's beats; the only route returning a Composition is POST …/versions/{n}/edits (src/app.ts:1156), which opens a draft as a side effect (review R3). Without this, the scene picker, Redo this part, CLI scenes and the MCP recipe would be empty for every version made before this plan. Review R8: ensureBundle reads AND writes Blobs (src/domain/bundles.ts:150-166), so the fill must check visibility first and only run for ready versions, never inside a transaction (review A6: no Blobs I/O while the job row is locked).

## Approach
- src/domain/beats.ts: fillBeats(deps, principal, jobId, n): Promise<BeatInfo[] | null>
  1. read-only visibility: loadJob outside any transaction (a private video the caller can't see, or a deleted one -> not_found 404, with NO Blobs call);
  2. version missing -> not_found; not ready -> 409 not_ready ('Version N isn't ready yet.');
  3. versions.beats set -> return it (no Blobs I/O);
  4. version.contract !== 1 -> return null with no Blobs I/O (it can't be scoped anyway; avoids unpacking every non-contract version on each call);
  5. else ensureBundle(deps, jobId, n) outside any tx (src/domain/bundles.ts:135), read index.html from the bundles store (blobs.get('bundles', bundleFileKey(jobId, n, 'index.html'))), beatsOf(...) (task 2.2), store with updateVersion(jobId, n, { beats }) (store only beats, never contract), return. ensureBundle null -> null.
- Route GET /api/v1/videos/{id}/versions/{n}/beats in src/app.ts, operationId getVersionBeats and x-sdk { resource: 'versions', method: 'beats', feature: 'scoped_revision' } (cli-and-sdk §4.1 and bead va-p1th.2.1: every route has both; the route only exists with the feature, so it names it; the coverage test refuses a route without them), response { beats: BeatInfo[] | null } (BeatInfoSchema in src/schemas.ts), errors 404 and 409 documented; same auth as GET video (Viewer+, API keys too).
- reviseVideo (task 2.3) and MCP get_video (2.6b) call fillBeats when the cached value is null.
- Logs: beats.fill { jobId, n, cached: boolean, filled: boolean, ms }.
This task needs 2.1 and 2.2 (beatsOf), not phase 1.

## Done when
Older ready versions return and cache their beats; no unauthorized Blobs work; no tx held during I/O.

## Tests
test/beats-route.test.ts (harness() = createApp(fakeDeps), memory + PGlite):
- a pre-plan ready contract version (beats null): returns the list and stores it; a second call is served from the cache (the fake Blobs records no get);
- a non-contract version -> { beats: null } with no Blobs call;
- a queued/failed version -> 409 not_ready;
- a private video the caller can't see -> 404 AND no Blobs call recorded; a deleted video -> 404;
- a Viewer can read; an API key of a Creator can read;
- fillBeats never runs inside store.tx (the fake store flags Blobs calls made while a tx is open);
- openapi:check and the operationId/x-sdk coverage test green; the spec's x-sdk for getVersionBeats has feature 'scoped_revision'.
- SDK refuses `versions.beats` with `unsupported_by_server` against a server whose features don't list `scoped_revision` (generated-SDK test with a fetch stub; no request is sent).

Standard: unit and integration with createApp(fakeDeps) (test/helpers.ts harness) and PGlite (pgStore(), every migration applied); Playwright on the mock build (VITE_MOCK=1) for UI; structured JSON logs (one event per step, with ids, durations and outcome) so failures are diagnosable from logs alone. CI (npm run typecheck, lint, vitest, npx playwright test, openapi:check, db:check) stays green. Repo rule: when checks pass, commit only your own files, push to main and confirm the Netlify production deploy is ready (other sessions often have uncommitted files in the checkout; never stage them).
